namespace Magma

/-- A member of the class, as the `7` orbit values it takes together with the proof that they name
one. `Magma.tupOK` is three tests: every orbit value is one the group's action allows, the operation
the tuple builds really is invariant, and no excess permutation is an automorphism of it. -/
@[reducible] def tup10R300 : Type := {w : Fin 7 → Fin 10 // Magma.tupOK S10R300.E S10R300.tr S10R300.z S10R300.st S10R300.X w = true}

/-- The class, as a family of magmas indexed by its own membership test. -/
@[implicit_reducible]
def srch10R300 (v : tup10R300) : Magma (Fin 10) :=
  Magma.mk (Magma.transport S10R300.E S10R300.tr v.1)

end Magma

/-! ### The source exhibits

`7` members of the class, chosen by greedy cover so that between them they model all `133` equations
that have a model in the class at all. Each check is `Magma.tupOK`: the tuple names a member of the
class. It is `decide!` rather than `decide` because the invariance test is `100` cells times the
`36` group elements, which the elaborator will not walk inside its heartbeat limit.
-/

